# Code owners — review routing for this repository.
#
# READ THIS BEFORE TRUSTING THIS FILE.
#
# A CODEOWNERS entry naming a user or team that does not exist, or that does not
# have write access to this repository, is IGNORED BY GITHUB SILENTLY. There is
# no error, no failed check, and no warning on a pull request — the rule simply
# never matches, and reviews are never requested. A file in that state looks
# exactly like a working one.
#
# This file therefore takes effect only if BOTH of the following are true, and
# NEITHER HAS BEEN VERIFIED from inside this checkout, because neither is a
# property of the repository's files:
#
#   1. The owner named below exists and has write access to this repository.
#   2. Branch protection on the default branch actually requires review from
#      Code Owners. Without that setting, this file suggests reviewers; it does
#      not require them.
#
# Whoever has admin access should confirm both in repository settings and record
# the result. Until then, treat this as routing convenience, not as a control —
# a rule the tooling does not enforce is a defect in this project, not a
# safeguard. See CONTRIBUTING.md, "Documentation is not a control".
#
# Placement: GitHub reads CODEOWNERS from the repository root, from .github/, or
# from docs/. This repository keeps exactly one copy, here at the root. Do not
# add a second one in another accepted location — a repository with two of these
# has one file that does nothing and no way to tell which.

